<title>USA: Texaco to take Iraqi oil if UN deal is on.</title>
<headline>Texaco to take Iraqi oil if UN deal is on.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Inc will buy Iraqi crude if the United Nations-Iraq oil-for-food scheme is implemented as many expect, Texaco's top executive said.</p>
<p>&quot;(We) will lift Iraqi crude if the (UN) oil-for-food deal goes through,&quot; Bijur told executives attending the company's annual analyst meeting at its headquarters here.</p>
<p>He did not elaborate.  </p>
<p>Under the oil-for-food scheme, Iraq is allowed to sell $2 billion worth of oil over six months in order to buy food and supplies for civilians suffering from sanctions imposed by the UN after after Baghdad invaded Kuwait in 1990.</p>
<p>-- Jim Brumm,  New York Corporate Desk +1 212 859 1700</p>
</text>
